id: pm-beads-tma4
title: Resume bounded Beads transfers with dependency closure and chunk receipts
description: "Add a dependency-aware transfer plan and resumable per-chunk application using public pm SDK capabilities. Overlap checked against the current CLI, pm-beads and pm-context: keep existing JSONL parser, structural validation and core transactions; do not duplicate neighborhood packing."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-24T11:13:36.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T11:34:56.299Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A killed transfer resumes without duplicates; A late cross-chunk dependency is resolved without dangling edges; Exceeding closure limits yields an explicit omission or refusal receipt; Concurrent drainers inspect and mutate state under the SDK writer lease; foreign records are skipped with reasons; all transition boundaries have interleaving tests on one non-git tracker; Typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON receipts, README and example, public tracker copy measurements, and npm plus Bun CI release gates"
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T11:13:52.625Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: registry confirms CLI 2026.10.24; this package retains its 2026.10.20 SDK pin. Existing Beads validation handles structural errors, cycles and aliases; existing import batches delegate core mutations. Core SDK exports commitItemMutations and commitWorkspaceTransaction with resumable journals; pm-context provides bounded neighborhood/delta packs, not a transfer ledger. Add only closure planning, immutable transfer identities and per-chunk receipts around those public coordinators. Use non-git trackers and deterministic interleaving at every package/coordinator transition."
  "2026-10-24T11:20:04.804Z",codex-agent,"Design refinement: dependency-first creation includes parent closure, so every published edge targets an earlier owned row even when its source record appears later or crosses chunks. The SDK transaction journal itself is the per-chunk checkpoint; no second mutable checkpoint store. Ownership comes from immutable create history, not copied bead_id markers. Skip foreign identities and their unavailable dependents, preserve peer edits, and never delete or close progress during compensation. The pinned bulk-create helper adopts any occupied id, so ownership-aware steps use commitWorkspaceTransaction plus PmClient.create instead."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:18.808Z",codex-agent,"Verification: linked command node --test test/transfer.test.ts test/transfer-cli.test.ts passed 11/11, zero skips, including an actual SIGKILL after durable creation and recovery after the SDK lease TTL. Same-tracker interleavings cover all 9 forward coordinator boundaries, all 8 compensation boundaries, both create boundaries and competing drainers before acquisition. New transfer module targeted V8 coverage: 100% lines/branches/functions. Existing smoke and flag tests: 117/117. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass; this repository has no separate lint script."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:19.863Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only buildPlan closure/order with selected-row-only batching makes both closure and cross-chunk drain regressions fail (0/2). Replacing only foreign ownership inspection with occupied-id adoption makes the foreign-record regression fail (0/1). Production source restored byte-for-byte, sha256 f427f51ed3407ffb07405f641126dd2eb8ef0bd581cfa4d625a6b05864017832; targeted suite passes after restoration."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:20.976Z",codex-agent,"Public real-data validation: read-only archived unbraind/pm-context tracker at c484938837a10e2b0963300d604c748e5c22f5f9, tracker tree d59e3c27dbd17ddbe71a0e5e1f1247321c74f6a6. Certified 89 rows, 58720 input bytes; all 89 transferred in 6 chunks with one real dependency edge, 0 duplicates/skips/dangling edges, 6 replayed chunks, and explicit maxRows/maxBytes refusals. Canonical plan 62173 bytes; compact JSON plan/resume receipts 712/3114 bytes. Separate public pm-beads run: 98 rows, 7 chunks, 8 parent links, 0 dependency edges, 0 duplicates/skips/dangling edges. Both archived copies stayed hash-identical and read-only; sources unchanged; execution used no git on PATH in non-git scratch trackers."
  "2026-10-24T11:29:22.066Z",codex-agent,"Operational boundary: this is creation-only exchange, not merging existing identities. Use reconciliation for incoming updates. Exact plans and SDK journals must be retained to resume; changed payloads or bounds create separate exchanges. A killed process may leave the core 30-second lease until expiry; busy is a typed retry receipt. Public SDK pin stays unchanged. Linked-test results are reported but tracker test-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy; results are recorded here. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to CI to avoid saturating the host."
  "2026-10-24T11:32:12.647Z",codex-agent,"Final ownership audit found a lifecycle interleaving worth testing: a peer can delete and recreate the same core id while history remains append-only. Ownership now uses the most recent create operation rather than the first, so a foreign replacement cannot inherit an earlier transfer creation marker. Added the same-tracker regression; foreign replacements and dependents skip without modifying the replacement."
  "2026-10-24T11:33:11.118Z",codex-agent,"Lifecycle experiment clarification: the public core correctly refuses recreating an identity with retained history (item_identity_reserved). No history was rewritten. The added regression instead uses an actual foreign create/delete tombstone: transfer now reads retained history even when its document is absent and skips that reserved identity and its dependent with reasons. This prevents a generic reserved-id failure and preserves peer deletion. Ownership also checks the latest creation record for defensive compatibility; source inspection failures classify the occupied identity as foreign."
  "2026-10-24T11:34:55.072Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification after the reserved-history guard: linked transfer tests pass 12/12 with zero skips, including SIGKILL and foreign tombstones. Targeted transfer.ts coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Reverting only the missing-document retained-history classification makes the new tombstone regression fail; production source restored byte-for-byte at sha256 2926d8a94801efeae21688b25234c8ec4f09f6ac22a84a5f2c8dca06b730e875. Both public tracker-copy measurements were repeated unchanged: 89/6/1 dependency and 98/7/8 parents, zero duplicates/skips/dangling edges. PR 165 is ready for review; waiting for npm and Bun CI gates on the final commit, without merge or release."
